(2834780, 394838, 22748, '<td valign="top">I like the lines on the ground leading your eye to the sphere. Good photo, I wish the background wasn''t busy, like if that fence was not there. Perhaps a higher vantage point (stand on a ladder?) would allow you to angle down more at the sphere and thereby exclude the fence from the photo.</td>', 'I like the lines on the ground leading your eye to the sphere. Good photo, I wish the background wasn''t busy, like if that fence was not there. Perhaps a higher vantage point (stand on a ladder?) would allow you to angle down more at the sphere and thereby exclude the fence from the photo.', '2006-09-14 13:17:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2834786, 395042, 22748, '<td valign="top">I think your biggest obstacle is going to be what appears to be on-camera flash. It makes really flat, bland, uninteresting lighting. Using existing light or off-camera flash would make the image more appealing. The "interesting-ness" factor of surfaces depends heavily on how they are lit.</td>', 'I think your biggest obstacle is going to be what appears to be on-camera flash. It makes really flat, bland, uninteresting lighting. Using existing light or off-camera flash would make the image more appealing. The "interesting-ness" factor of surfaces depends heavily on how they are lit.', '2006-09-14 13:20:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2834787, 393869, 22748, '<td valign="top">Nice composition, I like how you kept it tight and didn''t include any distractions.</td>', 'Nice composition, I like how you kept it tight and didn''t include any distractions.', '2006-09-14 13:21:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2834793, 395252, 22748, '<td valign="top">I love the composition; it''s really interesting and draws the eye in. However, IMHO the image is in grave need of some basic postprocessing such as Levels or Curves adjustments. A little more contrast and deeper shadows would make it feel much less washed-out. Another technique to try is called Local Contrast Enhancement: apply the Unsharp Mask tool to the image, setting the radius to a value in the 20-40 px range, and the amount to 20%-50% (threshold 0). Keep it up.</td>', 'I love the composition; it''s really interesting and draws the eye in. However, IMHO the image is in grave need of some basic postprocessing such as Levels or Curves adjustments. A little more contrast and deeper shadows would make it feel much less washed-out. Another technique to try is called Local Contrast Enhancement: apply the Unsharp Mask tool to the image, setting the radius to a value in the 20-40 px range, and the amount to 20%-50% (threshold 0). Keep it up.', '2006-09-14 13:25:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2834795, 395349, 22748, '<td valign="top">Great image. The gorgeous colors in the sky and the crisp silhouettes are nice. Cool title too.</td>', 'Great image. The gorgeous colors in the sky and the crisp silhouettes are nice. Cool title too.', '2006-09-14 13:26:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2834797, 394831, 22748, '<td valign="top">Nice simple study in shape and texture. I like the slightly contrasty look and grainy feel of the subject.</td>', 'Nice simple study in shape and texture. I like the slightly contrasty look and grainy feel of the subject.', '2006-09-14 13:27:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2834798, 395077, 22748, '<td valign="top">Nice simple composition. Simple in terms of no distracting elements (although I think actually the triangles could have made a great image without the lamppost too), and simple color scheme.</td>', 'Nice simple composition. Simple in terms of no distracting elements (although I think actually the triangles could have made a great image without the lamppost too), and simple color scheme.', '2006-09-14 13:29:28.000000', NULL, 1),
