(2835800, 394795, 53316, '<td valign="top">A very timely photo, and one that fits the challenge while telling a story: I see a lot of shots that just have shapes but no real sense of geometry, and this is not one of them, and the shot just seems very alive with the interplay of children in the foreground and the shapes in the background.</td>', 'A very timely photo, and one that fits the challenge while telling a story: I see a lot of shots that just have shapes but no real sense of geometry, and this is not one of them, and the shot just seems very alive with the interplay of children in the foreground and the shapes in the background.', '2006-09-14 20:36:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835802, 394701, 53316, '<td valign="top">I am going to score this highly.  I think that technically it is not a "good" photo, as shots like this really need to be in focus (I do adore the colors though!).  However, for this specific challenge, the out of focus works, for me.  It brings my attention away from "bug and flower" to "lines, triangles, circles, ovals."</td>', 'I am going to score this highly.  I think that technically it is not a "good" photo, as shots like this really need to be in focus (I do adore the colors though!).  However, for this specific challenge, the out of focus works, for me.  It brings my attention away from "bug and flower" to "lines, triangles, circles, ovals."', '2006-09-14 20:40:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835808, 393220, 64462, '<td valign="top">what school is it? Oswenzim High School? Or Buchenwald College? &gt;:(</td>', 'what school is it? Oswenzim High School? Or Buchenwald College? >:(', '2006-09-14 20:41:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835815, 395113, 53316, '<td valign="top">Oooh I have one of these in my front yard!  (<a href="//dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=296390" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a>)  They lend themselves quite well to odd perspectives, don''t they? :-)  I like the nice tones here as well as how you have balanced the subject against the sky.</td>', 'Oooh I have one of these in my front yard!  (here)  They lend themselves quite well to odd perspectives, don''t they? :-)  I like the nice tones here as well as how you have balanced the subject against the sky.', '2006-09-14 20:43:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835824, 394806, 54728, '<td valign="top">Nice blue...i''m curious about the faint square inside the circle.  I guess you darkened it on purpose, so they wouldn''t be apparent?</td>', 'Nice blue...i''m curious about the faint square inside the circle.  I guess you darkened it on purpose, so they wouldn''t be apparent?', '2006-09-14 20:49:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(2835826, 394950, 64462, '<td valign="top">i wish the crop were a bit, 3 mm higher, to include that... uhm..tack, and firing hammer would be lower.</td>', 'i wish the crop were a bit, 3 mm higher, to include that... uhm..tack, and firing hammer would be lower.', '2006-09-14 20:50:42.000000', NULL, 1),
