(2851643, 394680, 38234, '<td valign="top">Thanks Jewels.  That''s what happens when you enter too many contests/challenges/assignments on the same day with the same image:-((  I had the "valid" entry all ready and done up and the editing steps on a sticky note on my Mac - I just noticed after the voting closed which steps of editing I entered and realized (obviously way too late) what I had done - wrong image uploaded with invalid basic editing steps to match.  I''m pretty bummed out about it but what can ya do - just a stupid careless mistake.  What''s the real bummer is the valid one is as good with just a very slight difference as I didn''t use the multiply on a duplicate layer of the image but insteadit used a double curve adjustment layer and lowered the opacity of the second one:-((  Live and learn - I just have to be WAY MORE CAREFUL!!!!<br/> <br/>Thanks again for the kind comments!</td>', 'Thanks Jewels.  That''s what happens when you enter too many contests/challenges/assignments on the same day with the same image:-((  I had the "valid" entry all ready and done up and the editing steps on a sticky note on my Mac - I just noticed after the voting closed which steps of editing I entered and realized (obviously way too late) what I had done - wrong image uploaded with invalid basic editing steps to match.  I''m pretty bummed out about it but what can ya do - just a stupid careless mistake.  What''s the real bummer is the valid one is as good with just a very slight difference as I didn''t use the multiply on a duplicate layer of the image but insteadit used a double curve adjustment layer and lowered the opacity of the second one:-((  Live and learn - I just have to be WAY MORE CAREFUL!!!! Thanks again for the kind comments!', '2006-09-20 16:40:34.000000', NULL, 0),
