(2853245, 395260, 35720, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sigth:</b></div><hr/><i> hey!  that looks familiar! lol<br/> <br/>reminds me of mine</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Your shots are excellent Sigrún. The church is a great place and it''s possible to take many kinds of pattern shots of the ceiling in there.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-09-21 05:53:56.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by sigth: hey!  that looks familiar! lol reminds me of mine  Your shots are excellent Sigrún. The church is a great place and it''s possible to take many kinds of pattern shots of the ceiling in there.', '2006-09-21 05:37:50.000000', '2006-09-21 06:53:56.000000', 0),
(2853258, 393555, 30049, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by nova:</b></div><hr/><i> Good eye Barry to see that spider!  I don''t think I would have myself.  Wonder if you could isolate the area of the spider and bump the red channel way up to good effect...  Cool shot btw :o) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks Ray.  Being a basic editing challenge I was a little limited.  I did mess with color saturation some to try and get more emphasis on the spider but there is a fair amount of red (and yellow) already present in other areas (top left).  When bumped those other areas became distracting and competed with the theme of the image.  I almost kind of like the mystery it adds.  ;^)</td>', 'Originally posted by nova: Good eye Barry to see that spider!  I don''t think I would have myself.  Wonder if you could isolate the area of the spider and bump the red channel way up to good effect...  Cool shot btw :o)  Thanks Ray.  Being a basic editing challenge I was a little limited.  I did mess with color saturation some to try and get more emphasis on the spider but there is a fair amount of red (and yellow) already present in other areas (top left).  When bumped those other areas became distracting and competed with the theme of the image.  I almost kind of like the mystery it adds.  ;^)', '2006-09-21 06:08:37.000000', NULL, 0),
